Laravel Deployment on RunCloud – Quick Guide

1. Create a new GitHub repository (leave it empty).
2. Import official Laravel Git into your repository.
3. In RunCloud → Create Web App → select Git Deployment.
4. Enter your GitHub repository URL → select branch 11.x.
5. Save → Go to Deployment Script → click Deploy Now.
6. Create Database User → then Create Database → assign the DB user.
7. Add .env file with DB credentials.
8. SSH into server and run:
   composer install --no-interaction --prefer-dist --optimize-autoloader
   php artisan key:generate
   php artisan migrate --force
   php artisan config:cache
   php artisan optimize:clear
9. Fix permissions:
   chmod -R 775 storage bootstrap/cache
   chown -R www-data:www-data storage bootstrap/cache
10. Set Public Path in RunCloud:
    /home/.../webapps/<app-name>/public
11. Change PHP version of Web App to 8.2.
12. Visit URL — Laravel Welcome Page should load successfully.
